# cat(1)

## NAME

cat - concatenate files to standard output

## SYNOPSIS

    cat [-u] [file...]

## DESCRIPTION

Writes each file in order to standard output. With no file, or when a file is `-`, reads standard input.

## OPTIONS

- `-u`: accepted for compatibility; output is never buffered across files

## EXIT STATUS

- `0`: success
- `1`: an error occurred for some operand

## SEE ALSO

head(1), tail(1), tee(1)
